WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.970
<b>Conis</b>

3
00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:57.430
That thing? Are you sure you
want to bring it along?

4
00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.100
Uh, so... you don't
think I'll need it?

5
00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.310
Honestly, I'm not certain
you'll be able to use it

6
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.900
where we're going.

7
00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.030
It's up to you.
Do as you please.

8
00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.490
Huh. Thanks for
letting me bring it.

9
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.280
I just really like this thing.

10
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:31.750
Do you mourn them?

11
00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.040
Uh, no, sir.

12
00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.790
Heh. You don't have to put on
such a formal act, you know.

13
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.460
Express yourself, but don't make
the same mistakes as those fools

14
00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.820
who couldn't comprehend
the true power of God.

15
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.320
They took me too lightly and
so forfeited their lives

16
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.780
in the process. Their failure
was that their minds were not

17
00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.320
controlled by fear,

18
00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.830
and so they were not
prepared for battle with me.

19
00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.190
Do you understand?

20
00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.610
Yes. I-I suppose so.

21
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.250
I can't let him onto my plan.

22
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:11.080
I have no choice but to
obey everything he says.

23
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.750
An opportunity for escape will
present itself at some point.

24
00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.120
But until then...

25
00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.860
Where is he taking me?

26
00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.640
What's this?

27
00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.510
What do you think?
Amazing, isn't it?

28
00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:50.050
It's the only ship of
its kind in the world.

29
00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.930
And it can only be
controlled by me.

30
00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.980
In other words, it's powered
purely by lightning.

31
00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.340
Is that even possible?

32
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.360
But I assure you it is possible.
I channel my abundant energy

33
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.190
through a material that
can handle the power

34
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.490
and automatically transmit
it throughout the ship.

35
00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.950
What material could possibly
withstand that much power?

36
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.160
That's right.

37
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.670
The gold I have harvested from
this island works perfectly.

38
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.800
And I'm sure it will make many
inhabitants of this island

39
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.220
happy to see a flying ship
before their demise.

40
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.050
The sight of this
magnificent ship in flight

41
00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.930
will be the last thing they see.

42
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.420
A flying ship?
I don't believe it!

43
00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.000
If it really flies,

44
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.080
I might not have a chance
for escape after all.

45
00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.890
Behold the Ark Maxim.

46
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.660
With this ship we will reach the
land that knows no boundary.

47
00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.290
We will travel to the
Endless Vearth.

48
00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:49.040
We're outside.
We finally escaped.

49
00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:52.870
The ground is made
of stone. Where are we?

50
00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.370
What going on, Luffy?

51
00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.590
Hey, wait up!

52
00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.630
Luffy!

53
00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.770
We're free!

54
00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.110
We made it out!

55
00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.870
Woo-hoo! Where are we?
What are these old buildings?

56
00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.460
It looks like this could be the
place that huge golden bell

57
00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.960
is supposed to be.

58
00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:32.750
What is this place? Wait.
Could this be our homeland?

59
00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.630
But where'd that
big hole come from?

60
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.100
Luffy! Wait!
Where are you going this time?

61
00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.980
Wait for me!

62
00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:51.480
Hey, Zoro!
What's wrong with you?

63
00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.030
Come on, say something!

64
00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.850
How could this have
happened to you?

65
00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.370
How could any of this have
happened with you here?

66
00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.820
Nami! Where's Nami?
She's not here!

67
00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:15.670
Wyper...! Wyper, no!

68
00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:19.710
Bazooka guy was really strong.
But even he fell in this fight.

69
00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.710
Who could possibly
have done all this?

70
00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.800
It was Eneru!

71
00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.320
He's the only one who
could do something like this.

72
00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.770
Eneru, huh? That God guy?

73
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:40.950
Mm-hm.

74
00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.700
My Mantra didn't work
at all the whole time

75
00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.230
we were in the snake.

76
00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.500
So I don't know
what happened here.

77
00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:50.290
But I do know that it was
Eneru who did this.

78
00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:52.920
Robin!

79
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:59.170
Our Navigator.
She went with him.

80
00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.750
Just hang in there.

81
00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.050
It'll be okay.

82
00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.220
So you're saying Nami
was taken away from here

83
00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.050
by that God guy? Where?

84
00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:09.870
I don't know.

85
00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:15.540
Listen carefully. If we
don't do something, Skypiea...

86
00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:17.170
...will disappear.

87
00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.590
What? It'll disappear?

88
00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:24.340
My homeland will
be completely gone?

89
00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.180
Everything will fall.

90
00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:31.140
He said this nation in
the sky was unnatural.

91
00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.360
He said he'd send it
crashing to the ground.

92
00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.090
Eneru is definitely
going after the golden bell.

93
00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.990
He won't destroy this
place until he's found it.

94
00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.740
Right, and you have to stop him.

95
00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.570
But you must hurry because
there isn't much time left.

96
00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.980
You can't let Eneru
find that bell.

97
00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.250
Don't worry.

98
00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:01.910
I know where they are.

99
00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:05.280
There are only two voices
left on this island.

100
00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.540
It has to be Nami and Eneru.

101
00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.660
Aisa.

102
00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.760
I need you to take me
to them right now.

103
00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.370
There it is, Angel Island!

104
00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.340
Everyone, heso!

105
00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.720
The arch criminals Pagaya
and his daughter Conis,

106
00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.090
along with their accomplice,

107
00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:39.610
the former God Gan Fall,
are still on the loose!

108
00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.730
Please be on your guard!

109
00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.860
If anyone sees these fugitives,

110
00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:47.820
please alert me,
McKinley, immediately!

111
00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.870
Again, report any
news directly to me!

112
00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:54.750
In the name of the great God
Eneru, we of the White Berets,

113
00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:58.540
will defend the security of
Skypiea with our very lives!

114
00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.800
– Heso!
– Heso!

115
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.340
Captain! I have a report!

116
00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:03.390
Hm?

117
00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.750
What's the matter now?

118
00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:09.270
What? You say that
Pagaya's daughter

119
00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.190
has just been seen
in the harbor?

120
00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.070
The heretic has
entered through gate number one!

121
00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.890
I don't get it.

122
00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:33.760
Why'd she come back when
she knows she'll be caught?

123
00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:34.760
Don't let her get away!

124
00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.850
Capture her at all costs!

125
00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.540
Ha! Come on, criminal.

126
00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:46.510
Please make way!

127
00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.150
Move it! Outta my way!

128
00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:00.740
Wha...

129
00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.530
– Captain!
– Captain!

130
00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.330
– Captain!
– Captain!

131
00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.910
Oh no.

132
00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.550
Captain Mckinley!

133
00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.630
It's the criminal!

134
00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.420
Stay away!

135
00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.510
Judgment will fall on her!

136
00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.900
Look at all that gold!

137
00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:44.320
Remember your girl
friend from Angel Island?

138
00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.610
I've been listening and it
sounds like she's causing

139
00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.320
an uproar among
the citizens.

140
00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.070
Conis? No way!

141
00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.830
She should be waiting on
the Going Merry right now!

142
00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.000
There's a great deal of
noise outside at the moment.

143
00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:59.130
But no matter. It's hardly
worth mentioning.

144
00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.910
Uh, about this Mantra
ability that all of you

145
00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.450
seem to possess.

146
00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.040
Can you use it to locate
a specific individual?

147
00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.790
Not usually. Most of
us lack that ability.

148
00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.930
However, I can. I am unique.

149
00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.060
In addition to my
Mantra abilities,

150
00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.310
my lightning powers allow me
to pick up electrical vibrations

151
00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.650
and overhear conversations.

152
00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:29.570
When I hear someone
say something, shall we say,

153
00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:33.450
"out of line," I cast
my Judgment on them.

154
00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:36.540
The range of my hearing extends
over this entire land.

155
00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.910
So that's it.

156
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.960
It's a suitable talent
for a god, isn't it?

157
00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.410
Run as fast as you can,

158
00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:49.120
people of the sky!
This is Skypiea's last dance!

159
00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.420
A party of angels
dancing in the sky! Haha!

160
00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:56.500
You! Have you ever seen the
look on a mortal's face

161
00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.550
when he suddenly
loses his footing?

162
00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.310
He's out of his mind.

163
00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.210
What should I do? I have to
get away from here, or else.

164
00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.760
No. Even if I get away,
he'll destroy the sky island.

165
00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:13.100
There's got to be something
I can do, but what?

166
00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:19.190
I... I-Is there
something wrong?

167
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.570
Who is that?

168
00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.110
No, it's nothing.

169
00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:33.410
Please! You must listen to me!

170
00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.930
No! Get back, stay away!

171
00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:40.020
Everyone. You have to listen
to me! Please calm down!

172
00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.620
We don't have time to waste!

173
00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.190
You must hear what
I have to say!

174
00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:45.060
Get away from us, criminal!

175
00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.360
Leave this island,
you pestilence!

176
00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:49.900
Yes! You must leave now
or we'll all be destroyed

177
00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.360
when the Judgment
strikes you down!

178
00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.240
You heretic!

179
00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.450
Don't come any closer!

180
00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:07.920
This is a Burn Bazooka.
I'll use it.

181
00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.720
Everyone! You have
to go to Cloud End

182
00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:18.180
at the edge of the clouds
right away before it's too late!

183
00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:20.550
We have to escape
to the Blue Sea!

184
00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.550
This land is about
to be destroyed!

185
00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.090
There's no time to waste!

186
00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:28.760
Use every ship you can find and
leave Angel Island at once!

187
00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.270
What kind of lunacy is this?

188
00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.190
Eneru's planning to destroy
this land and everyone on it!

189
00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:39.730
If we don't evacuate now,
we're going to die!

190
00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.940
Ha! You're crazy!

191
00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.190
What kinda trick is this?

192
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.440
Is this revenge?

193
00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.580
That's nothing to be
joking about, you know!

194
00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.070
You think we're idiots?

195
00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.570
Don't talk
that way about Eneru!

196
00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.070
Oh, sorry.

197
00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:12.710
What? What's she doing?

198
00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.590
– Now! Arrest her!
– Yes, sir!

199
00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.800
Hear me!

200
00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:23.100
I refuse to accept
that Eneru is God!

201
00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.580
Father...

202
00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:39.950
She must be insane!

203
00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:03.240
That's strange,
the Judgment didn't come.

204
00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:04.660
But, why not?

205
00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.280
And after
committing such sacrilege

206
00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:07.990
against God,
I don't understand.

207
00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.660
Hey, what's going on?

208
00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.650
It's because
there's no longer any point

209
00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.410
in taking one life alone.

210
00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.540
"Skypiea is doomed." It's true.

211
00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.200
A member of the Divine Squad
escaped from Upper Yard.

212
00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.120
He risked his life to
deliver that message.

213
00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.920
He died.

214
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.320
He died with my father when
Eneru cast judgment on them.

215
00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:36.040
Did God do that? But why?

216
00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:38.950
I thought he was supposed
to take care of us.

217
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.260
What does that lady mean?

218
00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.570
There's no time left.

219
00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:46.400
We have to get to the edge
of the clouds at once!

220
00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:47.360
To Cloud End!

221
00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.120
No!

222
00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:50.770
Wait just a minute!

223
00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.360
We can't do it! We can't
just up and go like that!

224
00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.580
We were all born and
raised here in the sky!

225
00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.960
We can't live anywhere else!

226
00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.420
Yeah, she's right!

227
00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.230
None of us have ever even
visited the Blue Sea before!

228
00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.400
How would we be able
to live there? Besides...

229
00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.820
Then are you going
to stay here,

230
00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.770
doing nothing, waiting to die?

231
00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.880
We've all known for the past
six years what kind of a man

232
00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.590
Eneru is! Has he ever
shown mercy? Compassion?

233
00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.630
If he says he's going to do
this, then you know he will!

234
00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.280
Maybe it's not that bad!

235
00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.370
Maybe a miracle will
happen or something,

236
00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.790
and our island will be spared!

237
00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:26.250
Yeah, why not?
Maybe he'll change his mind.

238
00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.830
Yeah, yeah. That could happen.

239
00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.750
If we know anything
about Eneru, we know this.

240
00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.330
He's always had the power
to bring us to despair,

241
00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.130
to make us suffer
and break us!

242
00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:57.600
I tell you, what happens
now will make our past

243
00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.110
suffering insignificant!

244
00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.320
It's not going to do
any good sitting

245
00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.750
and waiting for a miracle!

246
00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.210
It's time to face the fact
that as far as this land

247
00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.420
is concerned,
God has abandoned us!

248
00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.960
Before we pray.

249
00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:11.130
Before we close our eyes to
what's really happening here,

250
00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:14.340
we have to do what we
can to save ourselves!

251
00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:17.750
We can't survive by hiding
behind his victims any longer!

252
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.630
If we do nothing, no matter
who we try to blame,

253
00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:24.970
we're all going to lose our
lives and it'll be our fault!

254
00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:29.720
Now. If we want
to live, we must leave!

255
00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.440
Oh, miss.

256
00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:46.490
Do you have any idea what
happened to the Divine Squad?

257
00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:47.650
My husband is one of them

258
00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.030
and I can't leave
the island without him!

259
00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.070
And my son's a member!
Is he okay?

260
00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.700
I haven't seen him in six years!

261
00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:54.490
Me, too. My only son
is with them, too!

262
00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.490
Um, I don't...

263
00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:00.160
The Divine Squad
may already be...

264
00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.240
I'm sorry. I don't know.

265
00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:03.880
What have they
been doing all this time

266
00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.380
on the Upper Yard?

267
00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.570
Are they still there?

268
00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.620
Can't you tell us anything?

269
00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.790
Please calm yourselves.

270
00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.450
I assure you the White Berets
will look into this matter!

271
00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.860
We will find your
family members

272
00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.240
and make sure they're
escorted safely to you!

273
00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:21.450
Now hurry! You must escape!

274
00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:22.740
But Captain!

275
00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.240
Move along!

276
00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.450
Captain, why?

277
00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.160
I can guess what will
happen to the Divine Squad.

278
00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.820
Eneru is that kind of man.

279
00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.580
I've always known that.

280
00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.330
But right now, our priority
is to make sure the citizens

281
00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:39.710
are evacuated as
quickly as possible.

282
00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:41.840
I won't let this
end like Birka.

283
00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:42.900
Birka?

284
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.580
It was Eneru's homeland.

285
00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.670
A sky island to the far
southeast of here.

286
00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.630
I've been told it
disappeared without a trace

287
00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.800
some six years ago.

288
00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.880
Wait. Six years ago?

289
00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.300
That's right.

290
00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.740
Eneru destroyed his own
homeland, and then came here.

291
00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:02.600
Birka was home to many
strong warriors,

292
00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:05.520
but they were helpless
before Eneru.

293
00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.670
An invincible God.

294
00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.780
I don't know,
maybe he really is.

295
00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.740
You might already know this,

296
00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:16.450
but we White Berets were
once in the Divine Squad,

297
00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.710
pledged to the service
of Lord Gan Fall.

298
00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:21.140
We thought that if we pretended
to betray the Divine Squad

299
00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.160
and swore our allegiance
to Lord Eneru,

300
00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.360
we could stay on the island

301
00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.060
and find some way to
protect the citizens.

302
00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:31.900
But, now it's all too clear
that plan was a failure.

303
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.460
We tried to keep anyone from
provoking Eneru's anger.

304
00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:38.590
We hoped that if no one
disobeyed him, they'd be safe.

305
00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.010
What else could we do?

306
00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:41.350
It was for nothing!

307
00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:44.850
For nothing! For nothing!
For nothing!

308
00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.230
It wasn't for nothing.

309
00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.490
After all this time,
I finally understand.

310
00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:56.070
Captain?

311
00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:59.520
Can... Can I count on you
to handle things here?

312
00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.860
Yes, but where are
you going? Tell me.

313
00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.690
Well you see,
there are some people

314
00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.570
who don't know how to escape.

315
00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.370
Some friends of mine.

316
00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.710
I have to go back.

317
00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.450
Take care!

318
00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.620
Of course!
The Blue Sea dwellers!

319
00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.080
– Heso!
– Heso!

320
00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.380
Heso!

321
00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:45.220
I won't be able to
move them all at once.

322
00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.600
We've at least got to
reach the upper level.

323
00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:52.020
Somehow, we must escape.

324
00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.720
Aisa!

325
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.050
You're sure it's this way?

326
00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:08.030
Yes! We're almost there!
I'm sure this is the right way!

327
00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.330
Good!

328
00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:15.250
That's it, Luffy!
That hole to your left!

329
00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:17.070
Over there! That's it!

330
00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:18.990
Then that's where we're going!

331
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.380
As I thought,

332
00:22:30.460 --> 00:22:33.170
they weren't among
the five survivors.

333
00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:37.460
Now where in the world could
they have been hiding?

334
00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:38.300
Could it be?

335
00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:48.690
How aggravating!
There's nothing I hate more

336
00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:51.030
than when my predictions
turn out wrong!

337
00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:58.660
Hey! Are you the
one they call Eneru?

338
00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:12.660
Luffy!

339
00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:17.120
If you mess with friends
of mine, then you mess with me.

340
00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:21.250
Hmph... Those fools
were your friends?

341
00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:24.290
You stay right there!
I'm coming up to kick your ass!

342
00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:26.300
Mind your tongue, mortal!

343
00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.050
You're speaking to God!

344
00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:30.630
What makes you God anyway?

345
00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:34.010
He's deliberately
picking a fight with Eneru!

346
00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:35.690
Be careful, Luffy!

347
00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:39.600
W-Wait, Luffy! Watch out.

348
00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:47.510
I can hear it now,
the angels' party!

349
00:23:47.580 --> 00:23:50.580
The citizens must have
learned of Skypiea's fate!

350
00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:54.350
I wonder how far they
can run before the ground

351
00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:56.170
gives out beneath them!

352
00:23:56.250 --> 00:24:01.220
I said, what makes
you God anyway?!

353
00:24:01.300 --> 00:24:02.970
You'll find out.

354
00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:10.230
Ah, I see.

355
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:14.900
You are no ordinary human, but
you're a mere Paramecia type.

356
00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:17.820
You can't beat me.

357
00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:22.400
Nothing that lives
can stand against me!

358
00:24:23.530 --> 00:24:25.660
That's why... I am God!

359
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:30.200
El...

360
00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.160
...Thor!

361
00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:34.580
No!

362
00:24:40.080 --> 00:24:45.340
Luffy... No.

363
00:25:02.710 --> 00:25:05.380
I'm impressed that you
managed to dodge it.

364
00:25:05.460 --> 00:25:07.670
Sixty Million Volts!

365
00:25:07.770 --> 00:25:09.610
He dodged it?

366
00:25:09.690 --> 00:25:11.490
Julungul!

367
00:25:25.290 --> 00:25:27.420
One hundred million volt.

368
00:25:27.710 --> 00:25:28.840
Vari!

369
00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:33.390
Of course!

370
00:25:33.590 --> 00:25:36.300
If I'd thought about it,
I would've realized it sooner!

371
00:25:36.390 --> 00:25:40.140
Lightning can't hurt Luffy,
he's made of rubber!

372
00:25:40.220 --> 00:25:44.770
I've had enough of you! Get off!

373
00:26:00.520 --> 00:26:01.820
Stay calm!

374
00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:04.450
Physical attacks still
can't affect my body!

375
00:26:04.530 --> 00:26:07.370
He's just a helpless monkey
from the Blue Sea World.

376
00:26:11.840 --> 00:26:15.720
His electrical powers
are completely useless!

377
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:18.840
Eneru must never have imagined
there was someone in the world

378
00:26:18.920 --> 00:26:23.970
who was immune to lightning!
It's incredible, but it's true.

379
00:26:30.770 --> 00:26:32.650
Luffy may be the
only person in the world

380
00:26:32.730 --> 00:26:37.150
who can battle Eneru.
They're natural enemies!
